      "side": 1,
      "message": "You currently use `static_cast` to extract the integer values from your strongly typed enums (`enum class`). C++23 introduced a much safer, expressive standard library function for exactly this.\n\n**Current:**\n\n```c\nreq_hdr.algo \u003d static_cast\u003cuint8_t\u003e(wrapped_algo_);\n// ...\nauto resp \u003d ec_comm.SendCommand(static_cast\u003cuint16_t\u003e(EcCommandId::kEcCmdGetVersion), 1);\n\n```\n\n**Better (C++23):** Include `\u003cutility\u003e` and use `std::to_underlying`. This prevents accidental truncation if the underlying type of the enum ever changes.\n\n```c\n#include \u003cutility\u003e\n\nreq_hdr.algo \u003d std::to_underlying(wrapped_algo_);\n// ...\nauto resp \u003d ec_comm.SendCommand(std::to_underlying(EcCommandId::kEcCmdGetVersion), 1);\n\n```",
