      "message": "All the places that need to change as generated by Gemini. Double-check for correctness:\n\n---\nTo replace the enum casts with `std::to_underlying`, you will need to update two files: `bootrom.cc` and `et171_flash.cc`.\n\nRemember to add `#include \u003cutility\u003e` at the top of both files alongside the other C++ system headers.\n\n### 1. `util/egis/bootrom.cc`\n\n**In `BootromComm::SendBootromCommandSha`:**\n\n*Old:*\n\n```cpp\n  SecureCommandShaHeader req_hdr{\n      .algo \u003d static_cast\u003cuint8_t\u003e(wrapped_algo_),\n      .payload_len \u003d ToLittleEndian(static_cast\u003cuint32_t\u003e(data.size()))};\n\n```\n\n*New:*\n\n```cpp\n  SecureCommandShaHeader req_hdr{\n      .algo \u003d std::to_underlying(wrapped_algo_),\n      .payload_len \u003d ToLittleEndian(static_cast\u003cuint32_t\u003e(data.size()))};\n\n```\n\n**In `BootromComm::SendBootromCommandAes`:**\n\n*Old:*\n\n```cpp\n  SecureCommandAesHeader req_hdr{\n      .algo \u003d static_cast\u003cuint8_t\u003e(wrapped_algo_),\n      .payload_len \u003d ToLittleEndian(static_cast\u003cuint32_t\u003e(data.size()))};\n\n```\n\n*New:*\n\n```cpp\n  SecureCommandAesHeader req_hdr{\n      .algo \u003d std::to_underlying(wrapped_algo_),\n      .payload_len \u003d ToLittleEndian(static_cast\u003cuint32_t\u003e(data.size()))};\n\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. `util/egis/et171_flash.cc`\n\n**In `ExecuteGetVersion`:**\n\n*Old:*\n\n```cpp\n  auto resp \u003d ec_comm.SendCommand(\n      static_cast\u003cuint16_t\u003e(EcCommandId::kEcCmdGetVersion), 1);\n\n```\n\n*New:*\n\n```cpp\n  auto resp \u003d ec_comm.SendCommand(\n      std::to_underlying(EcCommandId::kEcCmdGetVersion), 1);\n\n```\n\n**In `ExecuteBootLoader`:**\n\n*Old:*\n\n```cpp\n  auto resp \u003d ec_comm.SendCommand(\n      static_cast\u003cuint16_t\u003e(EcCommandId::kEcCmdEnterBootloader), 0);\n\n```\n\n*New:*\n\n```cpp\n  auto resp \u003d ec_comm.SendCommand(\n      std::to_underlying(EcCommandId::kEcCmdEnterBootloader), 0);\n\n```\n\n\u003e **Note:** There is one instance in `flasher_logic.cc` where you cast a raw byte back into an enum: `EgisCryptoType algo \u003d static_cast\u003cEgisCryptoType\u003e(fw[1]);`. This specific `static_cast` must remain untouched. `std::to_underlying` only extracts underlying values *out* of strongly typed enums; it does not convert integers back *into* them.",
