      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently, `BootromComm::GetBootromInfo()` and `BootromComm::GetFlashInfo()` parse the data into strongly typed structs (`BootromInfoResponse`, `FlashInfoResponse`) but then immediately print the results to `stdout` and return `void`.\n\nA protocol class like `BootromComm` should act as a pure data broker. It shouldn\u0027t know anything about console formatting.\n\n**Current (`bootrom.cc`):**\n\n```c\nstd::expected\u003cvoid, BootromError\u003e BootromComm::GetBootromInfo() {\n  // ... reads BootromInfoResponse ...\n  std::println(\"Bootrom Version: 0x{:x}\", FromLittleEndian(info.version));\n  return {};\n}\n\n```\n\n**Better:** Return the parsed struct. Let `et171_flash.cc` (the application layer) handle the `std::println` logic.\n\n```c\nstd::expected\u003cEgisBootrom::BootromInfoResponse, BootromError\u003e BootromComm::GetBootromInfo() {\n  EgisBootrom::GetBootromInfoCommand req;\n  auto resp \u003d SendStruct(req);\n  if (!resp) return std::unexpected(resp.error());\n\n  auto info_res \u003d ReadStruct\u003cEgisBootrom::BootromInfoResponse\u003e(*resp);\n  if (!info_res) return std::unexpected(BootromError::kResponseTruncated);\n  \n  // Fix endianness right here before returning it to the caller\n  EgisBootrom::BootromInfoResponse info \u003d info_res.value();\n  info.version \u003d FromLittleEndian(info.version);\n  info.max_cmd_size \u003d FromLittleEndian(info.max_cmd_size);\n  info.max_fw_upgrade_size \u003d FromLittleEndian(info.max_fw_upgrade_size);\n  \n  return info;\n}\n\n```",
