      "message": "In `et171_flash.cc` (`ExecuteGetVersion`), you manually `std::memcpy` the raw byte response into a `GetVersionResponse` struct. This is inherently risky. Because you already wrote the brilliant `ReadStruct` template in `egis_util.h`, you can add a templated wrapper directly inside `EcComm`.\n\n**Add this to `EcComm` (`ec_comm.h`):**\n\n```c\n  template \u003cTriviallyCopyable T\u003e\n  std::expected\u003cT, EcError\u003e SendCommandTyped(\n      uint16_t id, uint8_t ver, std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e payload \u003d {}) {\n    auto raw_res \u003d SendCommand(id, ver, payload);\n    if (!raw_res) return std::unexpected(raw_res.error());\n    \n    auto parsed \u003d ReadStruct\u003cT\u003e(raw_res.value());\n    if (!parsed) return std::unexpected(EcError::kResponseTooShort);\n    return parsed.value();\n  }\n\n```\n\n**Resulting Cleanup in `et171_flash.cc`:** This eliminates the manual memory copying, size clamping, and raw buffer handling in the application layer.\n\n```c\n  auto resp \u003d ec_comm.SendCommandTyped\u003cGetVersionResponse\u003e(\n      std::to_underlying(EcCommandId::kEcCmdGetVersion), 1);\n      \n  if (!resp) return std::unexpected(resp.error());\n  GetVersionResponse response \u003d resp.value();\n  \n  response.current_image \u003d FromLittleEndian(response.current_image);\n  // ... proceed with printing ...\n\n```",
